  "Name": "Kumar2015-TiO2-SiO2-480",
  "Source": "M. Kumar, N. Kumari, P. K. Rao, V. Karar, S. V. Ramagopal, and A. L. Sharma, \"Multi-layer dielectric thin-film optical filters for beam folding applications,\" Proc. SPIE 9654, 96540F (2015). doi:10.1117/12.2181776 - Sec. 2.1 text below Fig. 1 (p. 2): TiO2 56 nm, SiO2 92 nm; substrate BK7 from Sec. 2.2; indices Table 1",
  "Notes": "Five-layer TiO2/SiO2 folding mirror for blue light, peak reflectance at 480 nm at 45 deg (Multilayer I)\nSpecification: Peak reflectance at 480 nm at 45 deg incidence (beam folding, blue).\nReported: Text: peak reflectance at 480 nm (45 deg); TiO2-SiO2 multilayers peak 'close to 80 %'. Fig. 1 simulated (blue curve, read off the plot, approximate): R ~42 % at 400 nm, rising to a broad maximum of ~81 % around 470-490 nm, ~70 % at 550 nm, ~50 % at 600 nm, ~10 % at 700 nm. Fig. 3 measured (Multilayer I): maximum ~78 % near 480 nm, ~26 % at 400 nm, ~12 % at 700 nm.\nNotes: The paper says only '5 layered alternate TiO2-SiO2' for peak reflection; the HLHLH order (TiO2 outermost and on the substrate, 3 TiO2 + 2 SiO2) is assumed. TiO2 index is given as a range 2.2-2.4 at 550 nm; n = 2.3 (midpoint) is assumed, non-dispersive. Polarisation not stated; unpolarised (RA) assumed. Angle 45 deg in air. The simulation included the incoherent BK7 back-side reflection ('Any backside incoherent reflection was taken into account'), so the reported curves include the uncoated back surface. Total physical thickness 3x56 + 2x92 = 352 nm (not printed).\nLayers from Sec. 2.1 text below Fig. 1 (p. 2): TiO2 56 nm, SiO2 92 nm; substrate BK7 from Sec. 2.2; indices Table 1; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R peak 79.5 % at 483 nm, 45 deg, with the back surface; paper peak near 480 nm, R ~80 %.",
